[-] Implement semantic locations and bounded working sets =working-set $First walking slice: convert the accumulated observation stream into a bounded, restart-safe attention model before findings or Neovim. Acceptance: (1) surface current observations not cited by an active claim; (2) focus one with an explicit reason; (3) persist a semantic location carrying path, selector/symbol identity where available, revision, and relocation fingerprint; (4) rank and hard-bound the active working set without retaining whole-file payloads, with explicit omission counts and reveal; (5) show current/stale entries after edits; (6) restart and recover the same ranked working set and navigation trail; (7) project it through a thin Pi tool. Preserve native provider provenance; do not infer a universal symbol model or eagerly ingest the repository. Dogfood fact motivating this slice: run 13 ended with 166 durable observations but only provenance-oriented access, so the system senses/remembers well and still does little to direct attention.$ !1 +implementation ^2026-08-31T22:31 <kernel #01a05b73-6855-7791-83e4-0e7b6fcf9bb1
[ ] Implement findings and validation evidence =findings $Normalize diagnostics and command outcomes into a persistent quickfix-like queue while preserving native payloads, provenance, revision, dispositions, and evidence invalidation after relevant changes.$ !1 +implementation ^2026-08-31T22:31 <working-set #01a05b73-6862-7411-adb5-bd229ccaa248
[ ] Implement reversible change transactions =transactions $Add begin, apply, preview, validate, checkpoint, commit, and revert around Git-backed change sets. Associate intent, changed symbols, blast radius, findings, evidence, and residual risks with each transaction.$ !1 +implementation ^2026-08-31T22:31 <findings #01a05b73-686d-7523-a4d4-b5c4c7d741f9
[ ] Project shared workspace state into Neovim =nvim-projection $Create a thin human projection using native quickfix, signs, commands, statusline data, and semantic jumps. The shared substrate is authoritative; Neovim remains the human cockpit rather than the daemon.$ !3 +integration ^2026-08-31T22:31 <pi-interface #01a05b73-6884-79b2-a3af-4577cc07e03a
[ ] Dogfood the MVP and decide the next architecture =dogfood $Run representative maintenance tasks, record context churn, stale-evidence incidents, recovery quality, validation gaps, and human-agent handoffs. Use evidence to choose persistence, adapter, and collaboration scope for the next charter.$ !2 +evaluation ^2026-08-31T22:31 <pi-interface #01a05b73-6890-7991-a687-bd1eff659924
[ ] Fix the edit-time hook that reformats Rust files non-canonically $External agent-harness formatter drift remains active despite the repo's pinned rustfmt and check-only pre-commit hook. At least seven incidents now: runs 5 and 7 (twice) on tests/walking_skeleton.rs, run 9 on Pi TypeScript sources, and twice immediately after run-13 cleanup/commit on tests/walking_skeleton.rs (including a 36-line 12-insertion/24-deletion noncanonical diff). Each latest incident appeared between turns after a clean restore and had to be restored from HEAD; cargo fmt --check then passed. Rust is contained by restore + pre-commit + rustfmt-normalized workspace fingerprints; TypeScript remains the blind spot. Fix in the harness: disable edit-time formatting or invoke each project's canonical formatter.$ !5 +environment ^2026-09-01T19:18 #01a05fe9-40b4-7880-b405-ce1fbc0d8820
[ ] Fix Pi Lens stale diagnostic cache and disposition handling =pi-lens-stale-cache $Pi Lens continued reporting four impossible Pyright findings for .claude/hooks/orient-session.py after the source was fixed: line 131/154 findings on a 130-line file, duplicate main when only one declaration exists, and removed preview_index. python3 -m py_compile and the 16-check hook drive pass. Repeated lsp/full refreshes stayed stale, and exact false-positive dispositions (including reanchored lines/rules) did not remove the blocking mode=all cache entries. Reproduce and fix cache invalidation/disposition matching so stale intermediate-edit diagnostics cannot remain blocking.$ !5 +environment ^2026-09-02T11:13 #01a06353-172a-7240-97ea-ac52d873eec1
